-- title:
--   (3.17) gives (3.12): $\mathcal E_{t_i,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})]=\mathbb E^{\mathbb Q}[g(X_{t_n})\mid X_{t_i}=x_{i,j}]$
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $X$ is the recombining binomial tree of (3.11): nodes $x_{i,0}<\dots<x_{i,i}$ at time $t_i$ ($0\le i\le N$), up-probabilities $0<p^+_{i,j}<1$; $\varphi_{t_1},\dots,\varphi_{t_N}$ are distortion functions and $\varphi_{t_0}(p)=p$; $G_{i,j}=\mathbb P(X_{t_i}\ge x_{i,j})$, $G_{i,i+1}=0$; $q^\pm_{i,j}$ and $\mathbb Q$ are given by (3.13) and (3.15); and condition (3.14) holds.
--
--   Let $\Phi$ be a dynamic distortion function, $0\le i<n\le N$ and $0\le j\le i$, and suppose (3.17) holds at $(t_i,t_n,x_{i,j})$:
--   $$
--   \Phi\bigl(t_i,t_n,x_{i,j};\mathbb P\{X_{t_n}\ge x_{n,k}\mid X_{t_i}=x_{i,j}\}\bigr)=\mathbb Q\{X_{t_n}\ge x_{n,k}\mid X_{t_i}=x_{i,j}\},\qquad 0\le k\le n .
--   $$
--   Then for every $g\in\mathcal I$, on the event $\{X_{t_i}=x_{i,j}\}$,
--   $$
--   \mathcal E_{t_i,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})]=\mathbb E^{\mathbb Q}\bigl[g(X_{t_n})\mid X_{t_i}=x_{i,j}\bigr].
--   $$
--
--   Matching the distorted survival probabilities at the nodes is enough to turn the nonlinear conditional expectation (2.11) into a linear one under $\mathbb Q$, for every payoff in $\mathcal I$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a Markov process X on an abstract filtered probability space with transition law (3.11) and the filtration F = F^X it generates → the canonical path space Fin N → Bool (true = up) with path weights ∏ p^±, and X_{t_i}(ω) = x_{i, number of up-moves before i}; reason: every quantity in the statement depends only on the law of X and on F^X; the same instances
--   - encoding: times 0 = t_0 < ⋯ < t_N → time indices 0, …, N (Φ(t_i, t_n, x; p) is Φ i n x p, φ_{t_n} is φ n); reason: the times enter only as labels
--   - encoding: the assumption φ_0(p) := p → phiExt φ 0 = id built into the definitions; the value φ 0 of the given family is ignored; reason: the same convention, without a hypothesis on φ 0
--   - encoding: conditioning on F_{t_i} (resp. σ(X_{t_i})) and identities between random variables → conditioning on the atom of F_{t_i} containing ω (resp. on the event {X_{t_i} = X_{t_i}(ω)}), identities stated at every path ω; reason: F_{t_i} = σ(X_{t_0}, …, X_{t_i}) is generated by these atoms, and every path has positive probability, so almost-sure identities are identities at every path
--   - encoding: ∫₀^∞ Φ(s, t, X_s; ℙ(ξ ≥ x | F_s)) dx → Bochner integral over (0, ∞) of the same integrand; reason: the integrand is bounded with bounded support for every ξ the statement uses, so the integral is finite and equals the paper's
--   - generalization: the dynamic distortion function Φ constructed in the proof → any dynamic distortion function Φ satisfying (3.17) at (t_i, t_n, x_{i,j}) for all 0 ≤ k ≤ n; reason: the page's computation uses only (3.17), (2.11) and (2.3); the constructed Φ is an instance
-- source:
--   Ma–Wong–Zhang, Time-consistent conditional expectation under probability distortion, arXiv:1809.08262v5, https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.08262v5, proof of Theorem 3.4, display on p.14 ("by (2.11), (2.3) and (3.17)")

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DistortedCondExp_Distortion
import Definitions.Def_DistortedCondExp_Tree
import Definitions.Def_DistortedCondExp_Dynamic

open MeasureTheory Set

namespace DistortedCondExp

/-- **(3.17) gives (3.12)** (Ma–Wong–Zhang, arXiv:1809.08262v5, proof of Theorem 3.4, display on
p.14: "by (2.11), (2.3) and (3.17), for any `g ∈ ℐ` we have
`𝓔_{t_i,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})]|_{X_{t_i} = x_{i,j}} = ∑_{k=0}^n g(x_{n,k})[Φ(t_i, t_n, x_{i,j}; ℙ{X_{t_n} ≥ x_{n,k} | X_{t_i} = x_{i,j}}) − Φ(t_i, t_n, x_{i,j}; ℙ{X_{t_n} ≥ x_{n,k+1} | X_{t_i} = x_{i,j}})] = … = 𝔼^ℚ[g(X_{t_n}) | X_{t_i} = x_{i,j}]`.
That is, (3.12) holds."). Under (3.14), let `Φ` be a dynamic distortion function, `0 ≤ i < n ≤ N`
and `0 ≤ j ≤ i`. If (3.17) holds at `(t_i, t_n, x_{i,j})` for every `0 ≤ k ≤ n`, then for every
`g ∈ ℐ`, on the event `{X_{t_i} = x_{i,j}}`,
`𝓔_{t_i,t_n}[g(X_{t_n})] = 𝔼^ℚ[g(X_{t_n}) | X_{t_i} = x_{i,j}]`.

**Formalization Note** `𝓔_{t_i,t_n}` is `condE` (2.11) on the canonical path space, conditioning
on `F_{t_i}`; "`|_{X_{t_i} = x_{i,j}}`" is its value at every path `ω` with `X_{t_i}(ω) = x_{i,j}`. -/
theorem condE_eq_condExpQ_of_eq_3_17 (N : ℕ) (x p : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ) (φ : ℕ → ℝ → ℝ)
    (htree : IsBinomialTree N x p) (hφ : ∀ n, 1 ≤ n → n ≤ N → IsDistortion (φ n))
    (h314 : Cond314 N x p φ)
    (Φ : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ → ℝ → ℝ) (hΦ : IsDynamicDistortion N Φ) :
    ∀ i n j, i < n → n ≤ N → j ≤ i →
      (∀ k, k ≤ n →
        Φ i n (x i j)
            (cprob p {ω : Path N | x n k ≤ X x n ω} {ω : Path N | X x i ω = x i j}) =
          cprob (qPlus N x p φ) {ω : Path N | x n k ≤ X x n ω}
            {ω : Path N | X x i ω = x i j}) →
      ∀ g : ℝ → ℝ, InI g → ∀ ω : Path N, X x i ω = x i j →
        condE x p Φ i n (fun ω' => g (X x n ω')) ω =
          cexp (qPlus N x p φ) (fun ω' => g (X x n ω')) {ω' : Path N | X x i ω' = x i j} := by sorry

end DistortedCondExp
